=== Stage 06B defect probes (starting SHA 7ba8cb8) ===

[REPRODUCED] F3a: activation.select runs WITHOUT any authorization scope check and attributes selections to synthetic "system"
    -> no-scope actor was NOT denied (status 500 — store execution attempted); selectActivation(input) has no actor parameter and audits as 'system'

[REPRODUCED] F3b: stream.inspect reveals stream identifiers belonging to other actors
    -> cross-actor stream id disclosed: ["stream-other-actor"]

[REPRODUCED] F3c: changeset.get returns ok:true with empty object for a missing changeset
    -> missing changeset read returned 200 ok:true changeset:{}

[REPRODUCED] F4: HTTP Idempotency-Key does not govern execution: same key twice creates TWO ChangeSets... (probe via run.cancel-free path: changeset.propose is state-changing)
    -> same key, different payload -> 2 ChangeSets created (no durable receipt exists)

[REPRODUCED] F5a: fabricated validation/simulation evidence (caller-chosen runId/outcome/timestamp) is accepted and authorizes commit
    -> fabricated evidence accepted; high-risk commit succeeds with zero evidence

[REPRODUCED] F6: two-operation ChangeSet: operation 1 applies, operation 2 fails -> ChangeSet stays "approved" with partial external state (no atomicity/resumability)
    -> commit failed op2; status=approved; partial external state applied (rel-ok-1 selected) with no durable applying marker or receipts

[REPRODUCED] F7: SSE emits undeclared "replay.bounded" frames and a "schema" field the validator rejects; wire frames have no exported closed validator
    -> server-emitted frame rejected by the contract validator ([{"code":"AGENT_STREAM_UNKNOWN_FIELD","path":"response.completed.schema"}]); undeclared replay.bounded frame emitted

[REPRODUCED] F8a: port() returns 0 (not the real bound port)
    -> port()=0 but the server actually listens on 54132

[REPRODUCED] F8b: SSE treated as PUBLIC when no durable turn row matches the stream
    -> SSE opened for a stream with NO durable turn ownership record (treated as public)

[REPRODUCED] F9a: turn inputSummary retains the raw prompt prefix (payload-derived retention)
    -> safeInputSummary returns raw prompt text: "PROMPT-CANARY-9f2a confidential patient record 8842"

[REPRODUCED] F9b: tool argument summaries retain argument values and key names
    -> safeArgumentSummary returns serialized arguments: "{\"apiKeyValue\":\"SECRET-CANARY-44bb\",\"userId\":\"user-777\"}"

[REPRODUCED] F10a: tool-bridge swallows ALL durable store failures during invocation transitions (safeStatus catch {})
    -> safeStatus catches every store failure; capability invoked even when terminal persistence fails (normal completion reported)

[REPRODUCED] F10b: canonical argument digest uses insertion-order-sensitive JSON.stringify
    -> same logical arguments, different key order -> different digests (43258cff vs 3fb75453)

[REPRODUCED] F10c: tool-call identity fallback derives from current time (non-deterministic)
    -> missing toolCallId falls back to a digest over {turn, capability, at: clock()} — unstable across retries

[REPRODUCED] F11a: non-object payloads are silently converted to {}
    -> non-object payloads silently converted to {}: string payload produced changesetId=undefined field error; array payload executed whoami (200)

[REPRODUCED] F11b: unknown payload fields are accepted (no closed command schemas)
    -> whoami executed with undeclared fields hostileUnknownField/another (no closed payload schema)

[REPRODUCED] F11c: Content-Type parsing uses substring matching
    -> content-type check is !contentType.includes('application/json') — e.g. 'text/plain-application/json' or 'application/json-bad' would pass

[REPRODUCED] F12a: hub mutates event objects shared between subscriber queue and replay buffer
    -> the delivered event and the buffered replay event are the same object (identity ===); pending coalescing mutates shared objects in place

[REPRODUCED] F8c: subscribe() DISCARDS remaining replay on backpressure instead of buffering
